From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset inbound state only on restart

Commit 42c4cf5d4828 ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Add support for smp2p v2")
clears the last handled value of every inbound entry so that the values
a v2 remote writes after a restart are seen as changes. The commit
message scopes this to a detected restart, but the loop runs on every
interrupt whenever the SSR ack feature was negotiated.

Every notification from the remote then reports each set bit as a fresh
rising edge. On SM8550 the ADSP notifies several times a second while
its sensors stream, so the q6v5 ready and handover interrupts fire at
that rate and log "Handover signaled, but it already happened" each
time.

Only clear the inbound state when a restart is detected.

Fixes: 42c4cf5d4828 ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Add support for smp2p v2")
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index af0ceeaf6..0d588688a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
